ation Details   \n| Attribute  | Value  |  \n| --- | --- |  \n| Base Model  | FlameF0X/TinyMoE-100m-2x8-retrained⟨53⟩  |  \n| Quantization Tool  | AutoRound⟨54⟩  |  \n| Quantization Scheme  | W4A16  |  \n| Quantized Size  | 84 MB  |  \n##   ⟨45⟩ Evaluation Results   \n| Task  | Accuracy  |  \n| --- | --- |  \n| hellaswag  | 0.2603  |  \n| mmlu  | 0.2292  |  \n| mmlu_abstract_algebra  | 0.2200  |  \n| mmlu_anatomy  | 0.1926  |  \n| mmlu_astronomy  | 0.1711  |  \n| mmlu_business_ethics  | 0.2700  |  \n| mmlu_clinical_knowledge  | 0.2113  |  \n| mmlu_college_biology  | 0.2708  |  \n| mmlu_college_chemistry  | 0.1600  |  \n| mmlu_college_computer_science  | 0.2600  |  \n| mmlu_college_mathematics  | 0.2200  |  \n| mmlu_college_medicine  | 0.2081  |  \n| mmlu_college_physics  | 0.2157  |  \n| mmlu_computer_security  | 0.2700  |  \n| mmlu_conceptual_physics  | 0.2596  |  \n| mmlu_econometrics  | 0.2281  |  \n| mmlu_electrical_engineering  | 0.2345  |  \n| mmlu_elementary_mathematics  | 0.2143  |  \n| mmlu_formal_logic  | 0.2778  |  \n| mmlu_global_facts  | 0.1800  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_biology  | 0.2000  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_chemistry  | 0.1872  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_computer_science  | 0.2900  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_european_history  | 0.2242  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_geography  | 0.1818  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_government_and_politics  | 0.1917  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_macroeconomics  | 0.2026  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_mathematics  | 0.2111  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_microeconomics  | 0.2101  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_physics  | 0.2053  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_psychology  | 0.1908  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_statistics  | 0.1481  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_us_history  | 0.2696  |  \n| mmlu_high_school_world_history  | 0.2743  |  \n| mmlu_human_aging  | 0.3094  |  \n| mmlu_human_sexuality  | 0.2595  |  \n| mmlu_humanities  | 0.2431  |  \n| mmlu_international_law  | 0.2397  |  \n| mmlu_jurisprudence  | 0.2685  |  \n| mmlu_logical_fallacies  | 0.2270  |  \n| mmlu_machine_learning  | 0.2946  |  \n| mmlu_management  | 0.1845  |  \n| mmlu_marketing  | 0.2949  |  \n| mmlu_medical_genetics  | 0.2700  |  \n| mmlu_miscellaneous  | 0.2350  |  \n| mmlu_moral_disputes  | 0.2486  |  \n| mmlu_moral_scenarios  | 0.2380  |  \n| mmlu_nutrition  | 0.2026  |  \n| mmlu_other  | 0.2330  |  \n| mmlu_philosophy  | 0.1865  |  \n| mmlu_prehistory  | 0.2068  |  \n| mmlu_professional_accounting  | 0.2305  |  \n| mmlu_professional_law  | 0.2458  |  \n| mmlu_professional_medicine  | 0.1801  |  \n| mmlu_professional_psychology  | 0.2516  |  \n| mmlu_public_relations  | 0.2091  |  \n| mmlu_security_studies  | 0.1878  |  \n| mmlu_social_sciences  | 0.2164  |  \n| mmlu_sociology  | 0.2438  |  \n| mmlu_stem  | 0.2169  |  \n| mmlu_us_foreign_policy  | 0.2800  |  \n| mmlu_virology  | 0.2590  |  \n| mmlu_world_religions  | 0.3275  |  \n| piqa  | 0.5468  |  \n##   ⟨46⟩ How to Use \n###   ⟨47⟩ HF Usage \n**Step 1: InstallAutoRound⟨54⟩**\n\n```\npip install auto-round\n\n```\n\n**Step 2: Load and run the quantized model**\n\n```\nfrom transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer\n\nmodel_name = \"TinyMoE-100m-2x8-retrained-AutoRound-W4A16-RTN\"\n\n# load the tokenizer and the model\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(model_name, torch_dtype=\"auto\", device_map=\"auto\")\n\n# prepare the model input\nprompt = \"Write a quick sort algorithm.\"\nmessages = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}]\ntext = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(\n    messages,\n    tokenize=False,\n    add_generation_prompt=True,\n)\nmodel_inputs = tokenizer([text], return_tensors=\"pt\").to(model.device)\n\n# conduct text completion\ngenerated_ids = model.generate(**model_inputs, max_new_tokens=512)\noutput_ids = generated_ids[0][len(model_inputs.input_ids[0]) :].tolist()\n\ncontent = tokenizer.decode(output_ids, skip_special_tokens=True)\nprint(\"content:\", content)\n\n```\n\n###   ⟨48⟩ VLLM Usage \n\n```\nvllm serve TinyMoE-100m-2x8-retrained-AutoRound-W4A16-RTN \\\n    --trust-remote-code \\\n    --dtype bfloat16 \\\n    --tensor_parallel_size 1\n\n```\n\nIf you encounter any issues, feel free to open an issue on the AutoRound GitHub repo⟨55⟩ or provide feedback on the Low-Bit Open LLM Leaderboard⟨56⟩.\n##   ⟨49⟩ Ethical Considerations and Limitations \nThe model can produce factually incorrect output, and should not be relied on to produce factually accurate information. Because of the limitations of the pretrained model and the finetuning datasets, it is possible that this model could generate lewd, biased or otherwise offensive outputs. Therefore, before deploying any applications of the model, developers should perform safety testing.\n##   ⟨50⟩ Caveats and Recommendations \nUsers (both direct and downstream) should be made aware of the risks, biases and limitations of the model. Here are a couple of useful links to learn more about Intel's AI software:\n  * Intel Neural Compressor⟨57⟩\n  * AutoRound⟨54⟩\n\n\n##   ⟨51⟩ Disclaimer \nThe license on this model does not constitute legal advice. We are not responsible for the actions of third parties who use this model. Please consult an attorney before using this model for commercial purposes.\n##   ⟨52⟩ Cite \n\n```\n@article{cheng2023optimize,\n  title={Optimize weight rounding via signed gradient descent for the quantization of llms},\n  author={Cheng, Wenhua and Zhang, Weiwei and Shen, Haihao and Cai, Yiyang and He, Xin and Lv, Kaokao and Liu, Yi},\n  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:2309.05516},\n  year={2023}\n}\n\n```\n\narxiv⟨58⟩ github⟨54⟩\n* * *\n_This model is part of theIntel Low-Bit Open LLM Leaderboard⟨56⟩ initiative._ \n\nDownloads last month\n    234\nSafetensors⟨59⟩\nModel size\n34.7M params\nTensor type\nI32 \n·\nBF16 \n·\nF16 \n·\nFiles info\nInference Providers NEW⟨60⟩\n Text Generation ⟨61⟩\nThis model isn't deployed by any Inference Provider. 🙋 Ask for provider support⟨62⟩\n##  Model tree for LeaderboardModel1/TinyMoE-100m-2x8-retrained-AutoRound-W4A16-RTN ⟨63⟩\nBase model\nFlameF0X/TinyMoE-100m-2x8-retrained⟨53⟩\nQuantized\n(1⟨64⟩)\nthis model\n##  Paper for LeaderboardModel1/TinyMoE-100m-2x8-retrained-AutoRound-W4A16-RTN\n#### Optimize Weight Rounding via Signed Gradient Descent for the Quantization of LLMs Paper • 2309.05516 • Published Sep 11, 2023 • 13 ⟨65⟩\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨66⟩ Privacy⟨67⟩ About⟨68⟩ Careers⟨69⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
